3 Usage
*******

Open a buffer in one of the allowed major modes -- by default
‘org-mode’, ‘markdown-mode’, ‘gfm-mode’, ‘nov-mode’, or ‘eww-mode’ --
and type ‘M-x wordwise-mode’ (or your keybinding).  Uncommon words in
the visible part of the buffer are annotated with a small, subdued hint
line above them.  As you scroll, newly visible text is scanned
automatically after redisplay settles, in every window that shows the
buffer.

   Cached definitions appear immediately.  Words seen for the first time
are queued, deduplicated, and fetched one at a time in the background;
their hints appear as the answers arrive.

   The commands:

‘M-x wordwise-mode’
     Toggle the hints in the current buffer.  Disabling removes all
     overlays and, when no other buffer has the mode active, shuts down
     the network connection and timers.

‘M-x wordwise-set-difficulty’
     Prompt for a difficulty level (1-5), then rescan the visible region
     with the new setting.  *Note Difficulty Levels::.

‘M-x wordwise-ignore-word’
     Add the word at point to ‘wordwise-ignored-words’ and remove its
     annotation.  The word is saved through Customize, so it stays
     ignored in future sessions.

‘M-x wordwise-clear-cache’
     Empty the definition cache, cancel in-flight requests, and
     re-annotate the active buffers from scratch.


